<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lunéville</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lunéville is a town on the Meurthe in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meurthe-et-moselle">Meurthe-et-Moselle</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> of north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>. Duke Leopold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a> built a large palace there from 1703, inspired by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, and it remained the court of the dukes and then of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanislaw-leszczynski">Stanisław Leszczyński</a> until 1766. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-luneville">Treaty of Lunéville</a> between France and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> was signed in the town in 1801.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/luneville.jpg" alt="Lunéville" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Clément293 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:D0A3329-Modifier.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
